I'll preface this review by saying that  on the whole I disliked the DC animated  movies there are some absolute classics  such as The Dark Knight Returns Batman  year one and flashpoint however the  quality of these can often be credited  with being straight adaptations of the  source material when DC play loosely  with their smaller screen works such as  The Killing Joke and the string of  universe movies I find these far  inferior in quality naturally I was  cautious when I saw the announcement of  Gotham by Gaslight standing tall is one  of my favorite Batman graphic novels I  was disappointed to discover that the  piece would take elements from the  original work but massively subvert them  upon initial reviews cite their  disappointment for the piece I felt like  it would be another crushing blow to the  declining DC Animated work however I'm  happy to say that I thoroughly enjoyed  it perfectly capturing the essence of  Victorian London Gotham feels like a  living and breathing cess pit from the  dialog to the fog ridden streets every  aspect of the world feels authentic  while it's in the past I criticize the  other animated movies for subverting the  original pieces the changes here are  used to expand the universe instead of  changing it overtly every member of the  cast is a stellar job of bringing their  character to light and Bruce Greenwood  is very deserving of his place as the  voice of The Dark Knight  some characters are deliberately changed  for example Selina Kyle is no longer a  cat burglar but on the whole these  changes feel necessary in order for the  players to fit cohesively into the  storyline however there is one big  archetype twist for a Batman mainstay  that I believe will either make or break  the movie for most diehard fans will  probably detest this and it is difficult  to decipher exactly what the thinking  was behind this especially knowing that  it wouldn't be that well-received down  the line  I knew the plot twist going in so it  wasn't too shocking for me and over time  it has sat with me well in contrast  though those not prepared may find it  rather jarring and head-scratching  another peculiar decision is the film's  r-rating whilst the themes of murdering  prostitutes should never be aimed  towards children there is a certain lack  of weight to the actual killing scenes  themselves and it feels like the  creative team deliberately pulled their  punches the camera often pulls away and  never really  focuses too much on the diabolical deeds  of the mass murderer Jack the Ripper is  arguably the most famous serial killer  of all time so it seems strange that a  work centered around his face off with  one of Comics darkest creations would be  so censored the showdown is enthralling  though and it's nice to see those two  mainstays of fiction facing off against  one another  my final criticism towards the film is  that it's quite shallow in its portrayal  of women bar Selena Kyle and Leslie  Thompkins the female seem  one-dimensional and objectified sure  they are prostitutes but this is the  perfect platform to comment on the  recent sexual harassment allegations  that have been rampant in Hollywood  women should be explored as more than  stereotypes but they are limited in  their portrayal all of the problems I  had with the film are expected though  and as an hour and 15 minute piece the  team is a brilliant job of reimagining  the graphic novel I'm happy to say that  I found Gotham by Gaslight flawed but  enjoyable the film feels like a step in  the right direction for the animated  universe and there are several  highlights and red herrings here that  will keep you guessing throughout even  if you know the source materials outcome  perfectly capturing the Gotham by  Gaslight aesthetic this is a must-see  for fans of the Caped Crusader it melds  together the world of Batman and Jack  the Ripper and there's a lot more good  than it does bad Gotham by Gaslight is  definitely a movie that I will go back  to down the line and that's why I'm  giving it an 8 out of 10 so what did do  you think of Batman Gotham by Gaslight  comment below let me know and check out  my review of the original graphic novel  Batman Gotham by Gaslight in the  description thanks very much you better  subscribe I'll knock it out Cheers  you
 

